@161 = "Weapon Style Rebalance – Single-Weapon Style:
Rank 1: +2 to attack speed; one melee attack per round performs a weak grip throw attempt, briefly knocking down, holding, or immobilizing the enemy (ineffective against some enemies), also imposing -2 penalty to THAC0 and AC. Additionally, when in single combat (no other enemies within 4 feet), +1 bonus to THAC0 and AC.
Rank 2: +4 to attack speed; +0.5 attack per round; one melee attack per round performs a strong grip throw attempt, briefly knocking down, stunning, or immobilizing the enemy (ineffective against some enemies), imposing -4 penalty to THAC0 and AC, and 10% chance to disarm the enemy (humanoids only). Also, when in single combat, +2 bonus to THAC0 and AC.
grip throw requires a strength comparison (seven tiers: ≤13/16/18/20/22/24/25). It works only if the enemy's strength tier does not exceed the attacker's, and the enemy must save vs. polymorph (initial +6 bonus, +1 save difficulty per 4 character levels; thieves, bards, and monks get an additional save vs. death if they fail the first).
If the grip throw succeeds or the enemy is already incapacitated (stunned/held/immobilized), additional grip throws can be performed in the same round with no per-round limit.
Hasted characters get two grip throw attempts per round."
@162 = "Weapon Style Rebalance – Two-Handed Weapon Style:
Rank 1: +0.5 attack per round.
Rank 2: +1 attack per round.
Strength damage bonus is increased by 50%."
@163 = "Weapon Style Rebalance – Two-Weapon Style:
-0.5 attack per round, unless 5 proficiency ranks are invested (requires higher weapon style proficiency ranks enabled).
Rank 0: -2 weapon damage.
Rank 1: -2 weapon damage, +1 bonus to AC vs. melee.
Rank 2: -1 weapon damage, +2 bonus to AC vs. melee.
Rank 3: No damage penalty, +2 bonus to AC vs. melee."
@164 = "Weapon Style Rebalance – Sword and Shield Style:
The first attack each round is a sudden strike with +2 bonus to THAC0.
Rank 1: +1 bonus to AC vs. melee; one extra shield bash per round that briefly reduces enemy AC by 2 and knocks back. Enemy saves vs. breath to negate.
Rank 2: +2 bonus to AC vs. melee; one extra shield bash per round that stuns and deals 1d4 + strength modifier blunt damage (save vs. breath negates stun but still suffers knockback and AC penalty).
Hasted characters get two sudden strikes and two shield bashes per round.
Sudden strike and shield bash also work with thrown weapons (e.g., throwing axes, knives) but not bows or crossbows."
@165 = "Weapon Style Rebalance – Monk:
Monks have two grip throw attempts per round, but cannot perform them while dual-wielding.
When using a single weapon (one- or two-handed), they perform a weak grip throw (as Single-Weapon rank 1).
When unarmed, they perform a strong grip throw (as Single-Weapon rank 2).
Grip throw mechanics are the same as @161, but strength tiers are five levels: ≤13/16/19/22/25."
@166 = "Weapon Style Rebalance – Two-Weapon Style (requires EEex support):
The main hand suffers -0.5 attack per round.
Rank 0: -2 weapon damage.
Rank 1: -2 weapon damage, +1 bonus to AC vs. melee.
Rank 2: -1 weapon damage, +2 bonus to AC vs. melee.
Rank 3: No damage penalty, +2 bonus to AC vs. melee.
If 5 proficiency ranks are invested in Two-Weapon Style (requires higher weapon style proficiency ranks enabled), the off-hand gains +1 attack per round, +2 when hasted (simulated but not actual extra attacks, triggered on successful main-hand hits)."

@171 = "Weapon Detail Adjustments – Light Weapons:
Wielding a one-handed light weapon (dagger, short sword, wakizashi, etc.) or unarmed, with the other hand holding a shield or empty, add Dexterity modifier to THAC0 (bonus: 1/2/3/4/5 at Dex 16/17/19/21/24). If the other hand also holds a weapon, no Dex bonus but gain +1 to melee AC and off-hand THAC0.
Wielding a two-handed light weapon (spear, quarterstaff), gain +1 to melee AC and THAC0."
@172 = "Weapon Detail Adjustments – Long-Bladed Weapons:
Wielding a one-handed long-bladed weapon (scimitar, long sword, bastard sword, katana, etc.) with off-hand empty: 50% chance per hit to perform a small area cleave (1d6 + 50% Strength mod slashing damage, does not hit primary target or allies). With off-hand occupied, chance halved.
Wielding a two-handed long-bladed weapon (two-handed sword, two-handed katana, etc.): 50% chance per hit for a larger area cleave (1d10 + 50% Strength mod slashing damage; note two-handed Strength bonus is already 150%, so actual damage bonus is 75% of original Strength mod). Halberds also have area cleave but at half probability."
@173 = "Weapon Detail Adjustments – Bludgeoning Weapons:
Wielding a one-handed bludgeoning weapon (war hammer, mace, flail, morning star, etc.) with off-hand empty: one stunning blow per round that briefly stuns (duration: 0.5 + Strength to-hit modifier/2 seconds; 25 Str = 4 sec, 7 Str = 0), reduces AC by 2, and knocks back. Save vs. breath negates all. With off-hand occupied, chance halved.
Wielding a two-handed hammer: one stunning blow per round with 1.5x stun duration; even on successful save, enemy still suffers AC penalty and knockback.
Axes can also perform stunning blows but at half probability.
Enemy save vs. breath with +6 bonus (-1 penalty per 4 attacker levels).
Hasted characters get two stunning blows per round."
@174 = "Weapon Detail Adjustments – Hooking Weapons:
Wielding a one-handed hooking weapon (axe, etc.) with off-hand empty: 0.5 melee attack per round that hooks and drags the enemy's weapon or limb, causing a temporary loss of balance (-4 penalty to THAC0 and AC) unless the enemy saves vs. breath. With off-hand occupied, chance halved.
Wielding a two-handed hooking weapon (halberd, two-handed axe): 0.5 melee attack per round that hooks and drags; if the enemy fails the save, they fall to the ground and suffer -4 penalty to THAC0 and AC, with a 10% chance to be disarmed (humanoids only).
Hooking requires a strength comparison (seven tiers: ≤13/16/18/20/22/24/25). It works only if the enemy's strength tier does not exceed the attacker's, and the enemy must save vs. polymorph (initial +6 bonus, +1 save difficulty per 4 character levels; thieves, bards, and monks get an additional save vs. death if they fail the first).
Grip Throw and Hook cannot be performed simultaneously; if the Grip Throw fails, a hook attempt may trigger on the next attack.
Hasted characters gain two hook attempts per round."
@175 = "Weapon Detail Adjustments – Piercing Weapons:
Wielding a one-handed piercing weapon (dagger, short sword, wakizashi, etc.) with off-hand empty: one attack per round that causes bleeding for 4 rounds (1 piercing damage per round, save vs. breath negates) and has (Strength to-hit modifier +1)*8% chance to paralyze for 1 round (save vs. death negates; 25 Str = 64%, 7 Str = 0).
Wielding a two-handed piercing weapon (spear, etc.): bleed for 2 damage per round, and (Strength to-hit mod +1)*12% chance to paralyze (25 Str = 96%).
Halberds have half probability.
Lifeless creatures are immune. Save vs. breath initial +6 bonus, -1 per 4 levels.
Additionally, two-handed spears grant +2 to damage always."
@176 = "Weapon Detail Adjustments – Long Stick Weapons:
Wielding a one-handed staff (e.g., Staff Mace) with off-hand empty: one attack per round that strikes limbs, inflicting -1 penalty to 1-3 randomly chosen among THAC0, AC, or movement speed. Penalties stack, duration: 0.5 + Strength to-hit mod/2 rounds (25 Str = 4 rounds). With off-hand occupied, chance halved.
Wielding a two-handed staff: -2 penalty to 1-3 attributes, 1.5x duration.
Save vs. breath negates. Constructs/undead and limbless creatures immune.
Hasted characters get two limb strikes per round."
@177 = "Weapon detail effects trigger normally when wielding a single weapon. When a shield or off-hand weapon is equipped, trigger probability is halved. When dual-wielding, the per-round limit is relaxed to about 1.5 triggers per round (about 3 when hasted)."
@178 = "Weapon Detail Adjustments – Long-Bladed Weapons (requires EEex support):
Wielding a one-handed long-bladed weapon with off-hand empty: one attack per round performs an area cleave that directly hits all enemies in the area (weapon's full effects apply to each, does not hit primary target or allies). With off-hand occupied, chance halved.
Wielding a two-handed long-bladed weapon: one attack per round performs an area cleave as above.
Halberds also have area cleave but at half probability."

@181 = "Current mode: When each weapon style reaches rank 2, it automatically deducts 1 rank (triggers in combat), but grants +1 bonus to THAC0, damage, attack speed, and AC vs. melee. If later raised to rank 2 again, no further deduction occurs."
@182 = "When Two-Weapon Style reaches rank 3, it automatically deducts 1 rank (triggers in combat). If later raised to rank 3 again (total 5 ranks invested), the -0.5 attack per round penalty is removed."
@183 = "You can choose to refund deducted ranks and disable Weapon Style Rebalance, but only if you have not invested additional ranks beyond the deducted rank; otherwise there is no slot to place the refunded rank."
@184 = "When Two-Weapon Style reaches rank 3, it automatically deducts 1 rank (triggers in combat). If later raised to rank 3 again (total 5 ranks invested), the main hand suffers -0.5 attack per round but the off-hand gains +1 attack per round (requires EEex support)."

@186 = "Current mode actually increases the proficiency rank cap (may have compatibility issues if Kit or rule-adjusting MODs are installed later). Two-Weapon Style can be raised to rank 5; the other three styles can be raised to rank 3."

@191 = "Set whether weapon detail effects are affected by corresponding weapon proficiency (requires Weapon Detail Effects enabled)"
@192 = "Probability of weapon detail effects is proportional to the character's proficiency in the corresponding weapon: base 25%, plus 15% per proficiency slot"
@193 = "Weapon detail effects always occur (100%), unaffected by proficiency"
@194 = "Keep current setting (weapon detail effects affected by weapon proficiency) and return to previous menu"
@195 = "Keep current setting (weapon detail effects always occur) and return to previous menu"

